this looks good, but is there any way to do this within ObjectValuesExtensionBlock?  (big picture we're looking to get less special-casing of Block subclasses)

so maybe in ObjectValuesExtensionBlock could write

```
def _can_hold_element(self, element):
        tipo = maybe_infer_dtype_type(element)
        if tipo is not None:
            return issubclass(tipo.type, self.dtype.type)
        return isinstance(element, self.dtype.type)
```

?  Might need to check/test that this works for IntervalDtype too (wouldnt surprise me if we see the analogous bug there)

